WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:00:01.150 --> 00:00:03.650
Wealth, fame, power...

3
00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:04.440
Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates,

4
00:00:03.650 --> 00:00:07.820
Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates, obtained everything the world has to offer.

5
00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:07.360
attained this and everything else
the world had to offer.

6
00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:10.820
And his dying words drove
countless souls to the seas.

7
00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:11.660
What he said in his final moments drove countless souls to the seas.

8
00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:13.660
You want my treasure?

9
00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:13.700
You can have it!

10
00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:15.450
Go ahead.

11
00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:17.040
I left everything I gathered
together in one place.

12
00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:16.660
Find it!

13
00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:19.250
Everything is right where I left it!

14
00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:19.250
Now you just have to find it!

15
00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:23.750
These words lured
men to the Grand Line

16
00:00:21.670 --> 00:00:26.380
People set their sights on the Grand Line in pursuit of their dreams.

17
00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:26.920
in pursuit of dreams greater than
they'd ever dared to imagine!

18
00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:29.630
The world has truly entered the Great Pirate Era!

19
00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:29.850
This is the time known as
the Great Pirate Era!

20
00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:35.640
Come aboard and bring along all your hopes and dreams

21
00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:41.440
I know together we'll find everything we're looking for

22
00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:42.690
One Piece!

23
00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:52.700
Compasses? Not for me. Left them all behind

24
00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:58.500
I'm headed out to sea, with my heart serving as guide

25
00:00:59.330 --> 00:01:04.540
Following the ancient map to the spot marked "X" reveals

26
00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:09.760
Yeah, it's only legendary till someone proves it's real

27
00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:13.710
When the world's got you down,

28
00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:16.850
lean on your crew, they'll turn it around

29
00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:22.190
Their biorhythm will carry you through

30
00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:24.230
We're gonna make the most of it

31
00:01:26.110 --> 00:01:31.400
Come aboard and bring along all your hopes and dreams

32
00:01:31.610 --> 00:01:36.990
I know together we'll find everything we're looking for

33
00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:40.040
Got some change to my name,

34
00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:43.250
and maybe you wanna be my friend?

35
00:01:43.540 --> 00:01:48.130
We are, we are on the cruise!

36
00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:49.760
WE ARE!

37
00:01:50.050 --> 00:01:53.220
<b>Spin, Pinwheel, Spin</b>

38
00:01:52.690 --> 00:01:54.430
[BOTH] Big Bro won!

39
00:01:54.290 --> 00:01:59.430
[VILLAGER B] Arlong Park has fallen!

40
00:02:01.130 --> 00:02:02.660
Yay!

41
00:02:02.660 --> 00:02:06.660
Nojiko... Is all of this
really happening...?

42
00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:09.030
Surely this is a dream.

43
00:02:09.030 --> 00:02:12.150
[VILLAGERS cheering]

44
00:02:12.170 --> 00:02:16.990
[VILLAGERS] Luffy! Luffy! Luffy!

45
00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:21.040
Luffy! Luffy! Luffy!

46
00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:24.210
Good job Luffy! You almost
did as good as me!

47
00:02:24.380 --> 00:02:26.210
Let's face it I'm pretty much the star,

48
00:02:26.210 --> 00:02:28.380
but I'll cheer for you anyway
because I'm super modest

49
00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:31.090
and I don't wanna steal
your thunder! [laughs]

50
00:02:32.020 --> 00:02:34.380
[SANJI] You really had
us going there, Luffy.

51
00:02:34.390 --> 00:02:36.590
Start dealin' with
the bad guys quicker.

52
00:02:36.590 --> 00:02:39.850
I almost had a heart attack...
You rubber jerk!

53
00:02:39.860 --> 00:02:42.230
[VILLAGERS] Luffy! Luffy!

54
00:02:42.230 --> 00:02:45.940
Luffy! Luffy! Luffy!

55
00:02:53.150 --> 00:02:55.030
[USOPP laughs]

56
00:03:01.720 --> 00:03:03.080
[VILLAGERS] Luffy! Luffy!

57
00:03:03.080 --> 00:03:05.620
[LUFFY groans]

58
00:03:06.250 --> 00:03:10.090
[LUFFY laughing]
This is awesome!

59
00:03:10.630 --> 00:03:12.090
[gasps]

60
00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:25.140
Okay! Hold it right there!

61
00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:25.980
[VILLAGERS gasping]

62
00:03:25.980 --> 00:03:27.100
Damn! It's him!

63
00:03:27.150 --> 00:03:30.860
[NEZUMI laughs]
What a lucky day today is!

64
00:03:30.990 --> 00:03:32.060
Very nice!

65
00:03:32.060 --> 00:03:34.560
I saw the entire fight
and I must say, good work!

66
00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:38.910
I can only assume that your victory
here was some sort of bizarre accident.

67
00:03:38.930 --> 00:03:42.570
I never thought that the fishmen would
lose to riff-raff like you and your crew.

68
00:03:42.570 --> 00:03:45.500
However, now that Arlong
is out of the picture,

69
00:03:45.500 --> 00:03:48.450
I'll be taking all the money
I was supposed to give to him

70
00:03:48.450 --> 00:03:50.960
in addition to all the
treasure in Arlong Park.

71
00:03:51.420 --> 00:03:52.300
Now drop your weapons!

72
00:03:53.190 --> 00:03:56.970
Colonel Nezumi of Branch
16 gets all the credit!

73
00:03:56.970 --> 00:03:59.300
[screams]

74
00:04:00.060 --> 00:04:01.100
Zoro!

75
00:04:01.260 --> 00:04:03.220
I see you're trying to rain
on these people's parade...

76
00:04:03.220 --> 00:04:04.850
Now that's just plain rude.

77
00:04:04.850 --> 00:04:08.480
[NEZUMI groaning]

78
00:04:10.290 --> 00:04:12.220
[NEZUMI] Go on you scum...
Just try it...

79
00:04:12.220 --> 00:04:15.150
You'll be sorry! I promise you that!

80
00:04:15.360 --> 00:04:16.570
[SANJI] He's still talking?

81
00:04:20.680 --> 00:04:22.700
This is for shooting Nojiko.

82
00:04:22.740 --> 00:04:27.040
And also for mercilessly destroying
Bellemere's tangerine orchard.

83
00:04:27.040 --> 00:04:28.120
Huh?

84
00:04:30.840 --> 00:04:32.210
Colonel!

85
00:04:36.600 --> 00:04:37.800
Thanks Nami.

86
00:04:37.800 --> 00:04:39.300
That felt good.

87
00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:42.090
A thousand more and we'll call it even!

88
00:04:45.390 --> 00:04:46.520
[NEZUMI gasping]

89
00:04:46.520 --> 00:04:48.270
[NEZUMI groaning]

90
00:04:48.310 --> 00:04:51.410
What you're gonna do is
clean up after those fishmen.

91
00:04:51.410 --> 00:04:53.880
Then you're gonna help to
rebuild the town of Gosa.

92
00:04:53.880 --> 00:04:57.820
And you won't lay finger on any
of the money or valuables in Arlong Park.

93
00:04:57.820 --> 00:04:59.740
That's the island's money now!

94
00:04:59.750 --> 00:05:00.420
Got it?!

95
00:05:00.420 --> 00:05:02.490
Right! Yeah!

96
00:05:02.490 --> 00:05:04.390
I'll do anything you say!

97
00:05:04.390 --> 00:05:06.330
And there's one more thing!

98
00:05:06.330 --> 00:05:08.540
Give me my money back, jerk!

99
00:05:08.560 --> 00:05:10.790
I promise! I promise!

100
00:05:10.800 --> 00:05:13.670
I'll give every berry back!

101
00:05:16.820 --> 00:05:19.440
[NEZUMI] I'll get you, you pirates!

102
00:05:19.440 --> 00:05:22.470
Luffy is your Captain, right?

103
00:05:22.510 --> 00:05:25.030
Well mark my friggin'
words, rubber man!

104
00:05:25.030 --> 00:05:28.060
Major things are gonna happen.
'Cause you made me angry!

105
00:05:28.660 --> 00:05:30.430
I swear you'll regret this!

106
00:05:30.720 --> 00:05:34.190
I'll get my revenge!
Just you wait and see!

107
00:05:34.620 --> 00:05:36.690
[SANJI] Major things are gonna happen?

108
00:05:36.690 --> 00:05:39.880
[LUFFY] Yeah, how does he know I'm
gonna be King of the Pirates?

109
00:05:39.880 --> 00:05:42.950
That's not what he means at
all. Are you really that dumb?

110
00:05:43.070 --> 00:05:44.440
Hold on! What next?!

111
00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:46.530
Are we in super big trouble, or what?!

112
00:05:46.720 --> 00:05:48.870
Hey! Hey! What do we do?!

113
00:05:48.880 --> 00:05:49.870
[DOCTOR] Hey, everyone!

114
00:05:49.890 --> 00:05:52.890
Now's not the time to
keep this to ourselves!

115
00:05:52.890 --> 00:05:56.460
We need to tell everyone on the
island what happened here today!

116
00:05:56.460 --> 00:06:00.130
[VILLAGERS cheering]

117
00:06:00.130 --> 00:06:02.840
[VILLAGER C] Arlong Park has fallen!

118
00:06:03.570 --> 00:06:06.340
[LUFFY] Hey, Zoro,
what's that on your chest?

119
00:06:06.340 --> 00:06:07.810
Made ya look!

120
00:06:07.810 --> 00:06:08.970
[ZORO] Quit it, ya jerk!

121
00:06:17.280 --> 00:06:19.400
Good job, Nami.

122
00:06:20.820 --> 00:06:21.780
To think...

123
00:06:21.790 --> 00:06:24.740
Our island would be
saved by unruly pirates.

124
00:06:24.820 --> 00:06:26.740
The world is strange.

125
00:06:40.760 --> 00:06:43.420
[NAMI] Well, Bellemere.
We finally made it...

126
00:06:44.230 --> 00:06:46.930
It took eight long years
but we're finally free.

127
00:06:47.570 --> 00:06:48.800
The village... and me.

128
00:06:50.430 --> 00:06:52.180
[NOJIKO] Why are you still here, Nami?

129
00:06:52.250 --> 00:06:52.890
[GENZO] Huh?

130
00:06:52.950 --> 00:06:55.900
[NOJIKO] Your friends
have been looking for you.

131
00:06:58.350 --> 00:07:01.450
[NAMI] Hey, Nojiko. Genzo...

132
00:07:01.450 --> 00:07:05.780
If Bellemere were still alive and
I wanted to become a pirate do you think

133
00:07:05.790 --> 00:07:06.950
she'd let me do it?

134
00:07:07.290 --> 00:07:08.780
A pirate...?

135
00:07:08.790 --> 00:07:09.910
What do you think?

136
00:07:09.930 --> 00:07:12.540
Of course she'd never let her
precious daughter go out to sea

137
00:07:12.560 --> 00:07:13.970
with a bunch of treacherous pirates.

138
00:07:13.970 --> 00:07:15.900
– Yeah, she'd let you!
– [GENZO] Nojiko!

139
00:07:15.900 --> 00:07:17.870
But if she had said 'no,'

140
00:07:17.870 --> 00:07:19.880
that wouldn't stop you, would it?

141
00:07:21.430 --> 00:07:23.710
That's right. Nope.

142
00:07:23.710 --> 00:07:26.130
[NOJIKO laughing]

143
00:07:26.140 --> 00:07:27.840
[GENZO] I see...

144
00:07:27.840 --> 00:07:30.510
[laughing]

145
00:07:30.510 --> 00:07:31.850
What's up, Genzo?

146
00:07:35.420 --> 00:07:38.030
You certainty are
Bellemere's kids. Ha, ha.

147
00:07:38.030 --> 00:07:39.100
Oh, yeah?

148
00:07:39.100 --> 00:07:43.110
Nami, you've already made
up your mind about this.

149
00:07:44.870 --> 00:07:48.240
[GENZO] There's no use
fighting it. Live your life.

150
00:07:53.970 --> 00:07:54.950
He's still at it.

151
00:07:55.870 --> 00:07:56.620
[ZORO groaning]

152
00:07:56.620 --> 00:07:59.950
[SANJI] Well, you saw the way
he looked after that fight.

153
00:07:59.950 --> 00:08:03.210
[USOPP] Yeah, anyone
else would've been dead.

154
00:08:03.210 --> 00:08:05.010
[ZORO groaning]

155
00:08:05.250 --> 00:08:06.300
You dumbass!

156
00:08:06.550 --> 00:08:10.390
Did you think this
would heal on its own?

157
00:08:10.390 --> 00:08:13.470
Seriously, pirates are supposed
be smarter than this.

158
00:08:13.470 --> 00:08:14.720
[ZORO groans]

159
00:08:14.780 --> 00:08:16.810
[DOCTOR] Don't you have a ship's doctor?

160
00:08:16.820 --> 00:08:17.600
[LUFFY] Doctor?

161
00:08:17.620 --> 00:08:19.230
Never thought of that. Good idea.

162
00:08:19.320 --> 00:08:20.100
Luffy?

163
00:08:20.290 --> 00:08:22.310
But we need to get a
musician first, right?

164
00:08:22.310 --> 00:08:23.730
Why's that?

165
00:08:23.780 --> 00:08:25.910
Because pirates really like to sing.

166
00:08:25.910 --> 00:08:28.650
That's true, but why's that first?

167
00:08:28.560 --> 00:08:29.450
[NEZUMI] Hello?!

168
00:08:28.700 --> 00:08:34.160
<b>Marine Base (16th Branch)</b>

169
00:08:29.460 --> 00:08:30.590
Hello?!

170
00:08:30.590 --> 00:08:32.530
[TRANSPONDER SNAIL A] Yes.
This is Navy Headquarters.

171
00:08:32.090 --> 00:08:35.040
[NEZUMI] Headquarters!
Right! Good! Hello!

172
00:08:35.060 --> 00:08:38.830
This is Colonel Nezumi
of Marine Branch 16.

173
00:08:38.230 --> 00:08:41.960
Marine Code 00733!

174
00:08:41.460 --> 00:08:45.590
<b>Transponder Snail
16th Marine Branch</b>

175
00:08:41.970 --> 00:08:43.090
I have a request!

176
00:08:43.090 --> 00:08:45.670
There really is no reason
to shout. I can hear you.

177
00:08:45.810 --> 00:08:48.710
Listen! There's a pirate
who wears a straw hat.

178
00:08:48.710 --> 00:08:49.590
He's named Luffy.

179
00:08:49.630 --> 00:08:53.800
<b>Transponder Snail
Marine HQ</b>

180
00:08:49.710 --> 00:08:52.130
Listen! There's a pirate
who wears a straw hat.

181
00:08:52.130 --> 00:08:53.800
I hereby declare that he

182
00:08:52.720 --> 00:08:53.800
He's named Luffy.

183
00:08:55.740 --> 00:08:58.770
and his four crewmembers are
enemies of the government!

184
00:08:58.350 --> 00:09:02.730
<b>Marine HQ Information Office</b>

185
00:08:58.610 --> 00:09:03.400
I hereby declare that he and his four
crewmembers are enemies of the government!

186
00:09:03.370 --> 00:09:04.900
Luffy... Alright

187
00:09:05.130 --> 00:09:06.320
[NEZUMI] They managed to take down

188
00:09:06.340 --> 00:09:10.170
the purportedly invincible
fishman Arlong at his home base.

189
00:09:10.170 --> 00:09:12.910
Based on the grave threat
they present a large bounty

190
00:09:13.040 --> 00:09:16.330
has been placed on their
captain, Straw Hat Luffy.

191
00:09:16.330 --> 00:09:18.020
Transmitting photograph now.

192
00:09:18.020 --> 00:09:19.120
Roger that.

193
00:09:22.990 --> 00:09:23.830
[MARINE B] Huh?

194
00:09:24.130 --> 00:09:26.530
Couldn't you have taken
a better picture than that.

195
00:09:26.530 --> 00:09:28.340
No... Sorry sir.

196
00:09:28.340 --> 00:09:31.090
[TRANSPONDER SNAIL A] Okay, right
after a quick verification,

197
00:09:31.090 --> 00:09:33.300
I'll send it in for approval, sir.

198
00:09:33.890 --> 00:09:34.930
Good!

199
00:09:34.950 --> 00:09:37.970
Don't forget, he's a wanted
pirate! Dead or alive!

200
00:09:38.890 --> 00:09:43.520
I want his face on posters
all over the world!

201
00:09:55.920 --> 00:09:58.120
[SANJI] Boy am I stuffed.

202
00:09:58.120 --> 00:10:01.060
It's nice to not have
to cook for a change.

203
00:10:01.060 --> 00:10:02.960
So, how're you feelin', Zoro?

204
00:10:02.960 --> 00:10:04.060
I'll be okay.

205
00:10:04.060 --> 00:10:06.290
I think all I need's
a little bit a rest.

206
00:10:06.300 --> 00:10:07.710
That's good.

207
00:10:07.940 --> 00:10:10.920
[ZORO] Seriously, how much
longer can they keep this up?

208
00:10:10.940 --> 00:10:12.970
It's been three days now.

209
00:10:12.970 --> 00:10:15.590
Nothing wrong with that.

210
00:10:15.610 --> 00:10:18.010
Smoke 'em if ya got 'em.

211
00:10:18.980 --> 00:10:20.270
[LUFFY] Hey, Sanji...

212
00:10:20.280 --> 00:10:23.230
Where'd you get that melon you
had. I want to give it a try.

213
00:10:23.280 --> 00:10:25.600
It isn't polite to talk
with your mouth full.

214
00:10:25.700 --> 00:10:26.650
[SANJI] I dunno.

215
00:10:26.670 --> 00:10:29.070
It was a raw ham melon
with raw ham on top.

216
00:10:29.400 --> 00:10:31.990
[LUFFY] Raw ham melon?!
Show me where you found it!

217
00:10:32.010 --> 00:10:32.700
[SANJI] I can't.

218
00:10:33.240 --> 00:10:36.240
The whole town is basically
one giant buffet.

219
00:10:36.240 --> 00:10:38.030
Good luck finding it.

220
00:10:38.980 --> 00:10:40.040
He ran off.

221
00:10:40.280 --> 00:10:43.160
Three days of stuffing his face.

222
00:10:43.310 --> 00:10:47.380
And now that my belly's
full. Time to dance!

223
00:10:47.380 --> 00:10:48.840
With the ladies!

224
00:10:48.940 --> 00:10:50.910
[USOPP] I am Captain Usopp!

225
00:10:50.910 --> 00:10:56.470
I destroyed the strongest
of all the fishmen!

226
00:10:57.050 --> 00:11:01.270
Let's sing about me, let's sing!

227
00:11:00.580 --> 00:11:03.600
♪ I am the greatest, my friends. ♪

228
00:11:03.870 --> 00:11:05.480
♪ Oh, I'm the best that you see. ♪

229
00:11:05.940 --> 00:11:07.400
I'm so bored.

230
00:11:07.350 --> 00:11:08.020
[CHABO] Hm?

231
00:11:08.050 --> 00:11:10.400
I thought you'd be more upset.

232
00:11:10.420 --> 00:11:12.480
Why didn't this happen
before my daddy died?

233
00:11:12.620 --> 00:11:14.860
Why is life so unfair?

234
00:11:15.090 --> 00:11:15.820
That.

235
00:11:16.920 --> 00:11:19.410
I was kinda upset, at first...

236
00:11:19.500 --> 00:11:22.330
But I decided just to
think about my future.

237
00:11:22.450 --> 00:11:23.910
What about it?

238
00:11:24.710 --> 00:11:28.080
[CHABO] We were saved by the
straw hat guy and his friends.

239
00:11:28.320 --> 00:11:32.550
But tomorrow we have to start all over again,
on our own, without anybody's help.

240
00:11:33.040 --> 00:11:39.300
We can't forget the past... but... now...
it's... really up to us what happens.

241
00:11:39.310 --> 00:11:41.550
There's no one to blame
our problems on anymore.

242
00:11:41.550 --> 00:11:43.290
We can succeed or fail.

243
00:11:43.290 --> 00:11:44.930
It all depends on our choices.

244
00:11:45.610 --> 00:11:48.810
Whining about the past gets us nowhere.

245
00:11:49.190 --> 00:11:51.110
I decided to think that way.

246
00:11:53.270 --> 00:11:53.940
That so?

247
00:11:54.300 --> 00:11:57.260
Stop, ow, ow, let go, stop
that hurts, ow, stop ow!

248
00:11:57.260 --> 00:12:00.400
It's no fun if I can't harass
you for being a baby.

249
00:12:00.400 --> 00:12:02.330
So you decided to hurt me instead?!

250
00:12:02.500 --> 00:12:04.750
You stupid old punk!

251
00:12:04.750 --> 00:12:09.630
[NOJIKO laughs]

252
00:12:10.560 --> 00:12:11.750
Punk... That's right!

253
00:12:15.500 --> 00:12:16.630
[NAMI] Can you get rid of it?

254
00:12:16.630 --> 00:12:19.050
[DOCTOR] I'll do my best.

255
00:12:19.070 --> 00:12:21.350
But you do realize this is a tattoo.

256
00:12:22.420 --> 00:12:24.350
[NAMI] Heh. I was stupid.

257
00:12:24.620 --> 00:12:27.310
I knew it wouldn't come off.

258
00:12:27.660 --> 00:12:31.060
[NAMI cries] I don't
want anyone to see this!

259
00:12:31.060 --> 00:12:34.930
This... This awful tattoo.

260
00:12:34.930 --> 00:12:40.570
I'm just pretending but
it's like he owns me now.

261
00:12:42.360 --> 00:12:43.580
Nami.

262
00:12:46.260 --> 00:12:48.290
[NAMI] Nojiko, what is that?

263
00:12:48.290 --> 00:12:50.210
[NOJIKO] Oh, you mean this?

264
00:12:50.370 --> 00:12:53.710
It's nothing, just a tattoo.

265
00:12:54.010 --> 00:12:56.550
Now I look just like you.

266
00:12:56.550 --> 00:12:59.300
[BOTH laughing]

267
00:13:01.760 --> 00:13:02.590
[NAMI] Hey, Doc.

268
00:13:02.590 --> 00:13:03.600
[DOCTOR] Mm?

269
00:13:04.060 --> 00:13:06.520
[NAMI] I think I'd like a new tattoo.

270
00:13:06.530 --> 00:13:07.900
[DOCTOR] Hm?

271
00:13:07.900 --> 00:13:09.060
[NAMI] Like this.

272
00:13:10.230 --> 00:13:11.600
[VILLAGERS chattering, laughing]

273
00:13:11.450 --> 00:13:12.730
[USOPP] ♪ La... La...

274
00:13:11.600 --> 00:13:13.820
On to Captain Usopp song. Number 185.

275
00:13:13.820 --> 00:13:15.520
Let's stand as we sing.

276
00:13:22.030 --> 00:13:23.600
[GENZO] Bellemere.

277
00:13:23.600 --> 00:13:25.700
Your daughters are
strong young women now.

278
00:13:25.700 --> 00:13:26.490
You'd be so proud.

279
00:13:27.680 --> 00:13:30.210
It's like I'm standing
right in front of you again.

280
00:13:30.210 --> 00:13:34.040
[GENZO] We're not going to
waste a single moment now.

281
00:13:34.040 --> 00:13:35.630
So much has been lost.

282
00:13:35.950 --> 00:13:38.750
Everyone has had to make
terrible sacrifices.

283
00:13:38.750 --> 00:13:41.280
Which is why I don't care
if I look like a fool,

284
00:13:41.280 --> 00:13:44.430
I'm happy for the first
time in a long while.

285
00:13:46.180 --> 00:13:48.270
[LUFFY] Raw ham melon!

286
00:13:48.510 --> 00:13:52.190
Wha...? There's no food up here.

287
00:13:52.210 --> 00:13:53.900
Guess I'll go back Be quiet!

288
00:13:55.150 --> 00:13:57.460
[LUFFY] A grave? Did somebody die?

289
00:13:57.460 --> 00:14:00.400
[GENZO] Yes. A long time ago.

290
00:14:01.160 --> 00:14:02.770
Oh, I'm sorry.

291
00:14:02.770 --> 00:14:05.370
I give you to my conveniences.

292
00:14:05.670 --> 00:14:08.440
Wait, my sincere compliments.

293
00:14:08.440 --> 00:14:10.440
Nope... My darkest concussion?

294
00:14:10.440 --> 00:14:12.580
[GENZO] My deepest condolences.

295
00:14:12.580 --> 00:14:14.460
[LUFFY] Thanks!

296
00:14:14.630 --> 00:14:15.750
[GENZO] Listen, boy.

297
00:14:16.260 --> 00:14:18.170
I know Nami's going away with you.

298
00:14:18.600 --> 00:14:22.300
She has her mind set on becoming a pirate,
and that's dangerous business.

299
00:14:23.190 --> 00:14:27.100
And I'm fine with that.
It can't be helped.

300
00:14:27.460 --> 00:14:33.060
But if any of you ever do anything
to hurt her, I will kill you.

301
00:14:33.960 --> 00:14:36.020
[LUFFY] We're not going to hurt her.

302
00:14:36.630 --> 00:14:38.400
You sure?!

303
00:14:39.640 --> 00:14:40.440
I'm sure.

304
00:14:46.240 --> 00:14:49.490
<b>The Morning of Departure</b>

305
00:14:52.200 --> 00:14:53.960
[USOPP] This is the last one, right?

306
00:14:53.970 --> 00:14:54.640
[ZORO] Yeah.

307
00:14:54.640 --> 00:14:56.010
[LUFFY] We got everything?

308
00:14:56.010 --> 00:14:57.000
[USOPP] Yup!

309
00:14:57.140 --> 00:14:59.880
Alright. We're stocked up
with everything we need.

310
00:14:59.980 --> 00:15:01.090
I think we're good to go.

311
00:15:01.910 --> 00:15:04.230
[USOPP grunts] You know we've
only been on this little island

312
00:15:04.230 --> 00:15:06.590
for a few days but it feels
more like a lifetime.

313
00:15:06.680 --> 00:15:09.230
Yeah! [laughs]

314
00:15:09.230 --> 00:15:10.640
[SANJI] Hm?

315
00:15:14.830 --> 00:15:18.090
We can't thank you enough for
everything you've done for us,

316
00:15:18.090 --> 00:15:21.600
but we gotta go back to our
regular jobs as bounty hunters.

317
00:15:21.600 --> 00:15:22.900
So, this is goodbye.

318
00:15:23.500 --> 00:15:26.410
I hope we get to meet again someday.

319
00:15:27.210 --> 00:15:28.370
See ya 'round.

320
00:15:28.980 --> 00:15:30.310
[JOHNNY, YOSAKU] Goodbye!

321
00:15:30.310 --> 00:15:32.830
Yeah, now it's time
for us to get going.

322
00:15:32.830 --> 00:15:34.040
[gasps]

323
00:15:34.040 --> 00:15:36.370
But we can't leave yet...
we gotta wait for Nami.

324
00:15:36.380 --> 00:15:38.370
Well, maybe she's not coming.

325
00:15:38.370 --> 00:15:40.590
Uhh. What, why not?!

326
00:15:41.050 --> 00:15:44.800
If you try to hit on her again, I swear
I'll break your freakin' neck! You got it?!

327
00:15:44.820 --> 00:15:46.010
Why would I do something like that?

328
00:15:46.030 --> 00:15:47.430
[USOPP] She might not even be coming.

329
00:15:47.430 --> 00:15:49.210
After all, she has achieved her goal.

330
00:15:49.210 --> 00:15:51.210
Nami doesn't have to
be a pirate anymore.

331
00:15:51.210 --> 00:15:53.430
She might be better off if she
stayed here on this island

332
00:15:53.450 --> 00:15:55.100
with all her friends and family.

333
00:15:55.140 --> 00:15:56.980
What about me, dammit?!

334
00:15:57.000 --> 00:16:00.230
Without Nami onboard I have
like 98.72% less reason

335
00:16:00.980 --> 00:16:03.480
to stay with you people
on this stupid pirate ship.

336
00:16:03.480 --> 00:16:06.570
Hey, I'm still upset with you
about the raw ham melon!

337
00:16:07.600 --> 00:16:08.200
Nami here?

338
00:16:08.300 --> 00:16:09.280
Don't know.

339
00:16:09.370 --> 00:16:11.330
I haven't seen her anywhere
since this morning.

340
00:16:11.340 --> 00:16:12.010
[GENZO] What?!

341
00:16:12.010 --> 00:16:14.040
One hundred million berries?

342
00:16:14.150 --> 00:16:16.250
She left all of it in
our house with a letter.

343
00:16:16.390 --> 00:16:18.540
She's not even gonna take some of it?

344
00:16:18.850 --> 00:16:21.340
But she worked so hard to get it.

345
00:16:21.590 --> 00:16:23.050
She'll steal more.

346
00:16:23.130 --> 00:16:24.510
That's what her letter said.

347
00:16:25.800 --> 00:16:28.880
There's no changing her
mind once it's made up.

348
00:16:29.000 --> 00:16:30.260
That girl.

349
00:16:30.290 --> 00:16:33.970
She didn't even give us
a chance to thank her.

350
00:16:33.970 --> 00:16:34.850
[LUFFY gasps]

351
00:16:34.850 --> 00:16:35.720
[USOPP, ZORO gasp]

352
00:16:35.720 --> 00:16:36.890
[SANJI screams]

353
00:16:36.890 --> 00:16:38.480
[ALL] Hm?

354
00:16:38.630 --> 00:16:40.230
[SANJI] There she is!

355
00:16:40.230 --> 00:16:40.940
[GENZO] Nami!

356
00:16:41.120 --> 00:16:41.770
[NOJIKO] Nami!

357
00:16:41.820 --> 00:16:43.900
[VILLAGERS] Nami!

358
00:16:43.930 --> 00:16:45.530
Set the sails!

359
00:16:45.530 --> 00:16:46.530
[LUFFY] Hm?

360
00:16:51.790 --> 00:16:53.980
I don't get it. Why's she running?

361
00:16:53.980 --> 00:16:55.410
[LUFFY] She said to set sail.

362
00:16:55.410 --> 00:16:55.990
What?

363
00:16:57.620 --> 00:17:02.420
No, she's planning on leaving us without
letting any of us thank her or say goodbye.

364
00:17:02.430 --> 00:17:03.560
Hey, wait!

365
00:17:03.560 --> 00:17:05.380
[LUFFY] Set sail

366
00:17:10.490 --> 00:17:12.800
[VILLAGER A] Wait! Don't go!

367
00:17:12.820 --> 00:17:13.790
[VILLAGER B] They're leaving!

368
00:17:13.790 --> 00:17:16.180
[DOCTOR] Stop!
At least let us say goodbye!

369
00:17:17.960 --> 00:17:19.140
[VILLAGER A] Nami, don't!

370
00:17:19.560 --> 00:17:22.350
[VILLAGER B] Let us thank you!

371
00:17:23.050 --> 00:17:26.360
Nami! Come back here
you can't leave this way!

372
00:17:26.620 --> 00:17:29.560
So, you sure you want
to let her leave like this?

373
00:17:29.560 --> 00:17:30.990
Not my decision.

374
00:17:30.990 --> 00:17:32.320
She does what she wants.

375
00:17:33.210 --> 00:17:34.490
Nami!

376
00:17:34.490 --> 00:17:49.010
[VILLAGERS shouting]

377
00:17:49.840 --> 00:17:51.090
[VILLAGERS] Nami!

378
00:18:01.270 --> 00:18:02.100
Why?!

379
00:18:23.360 --> 00:18:24.460
Huh?! No way!

380
00:18:24.630 --> 00:18:25.670
[VILLAGER A] Hey, where's my money?!

381
00:18:25.700 --> 00:18:26.830
[VILLAGER B] My wallet's gone!

382
00:18:26.830 --> 00:18:28.050
[VILLAGER C] Mine, too!

383
00:18:28.070 --> 00:18:29.500
[VILLAGER D] She stole my money!

384
00:18:29.500 --> 00:18:32.050
[VILLAGER AA] My purse is gone!

385
00:18:34.210 --> 00:18:36.390
Thanks a bunch!

386
00:18:36.580 --> 00:18:41.480
Damn! You little brat!

387
00:18:42.500 --> 00:18:45.440
Great, she hasn't changed a bit.

388
00:18:45.470 --> 00:18:47.270
I'd watch my back.

389
00:18:47.270 --> 00:18:51.070
[LUFFY, SANJI laughing]

390
00:18:51.400 --> 00:18:55.160
[GENZO] You lousy pickpocket!
We'll miss you!

391
00:19:01.200 --> 00:19:02.700
[LUFFY laughing]

392
00:19:03.180 --> 00:19:04.080
[GENZO] Boy!

393
00:19:05.280 --> 00:19:07.920
Remember what I told you.

394
00:19:10.620 --> 00:19:11.790
[LUFFY] You got it!

395
00:19:11.790 --> 00:19:15.090
[NAMI] Goodbye everybody!
I'll miss you. Take care.

396
00:19:16.960 --> 00:19:20.060
[NOJIKO laughing]
I can't believe her!

397
00:19:20.130 --> 00:19:22.850
My little sister got
us good with that one.

398
00:19:24.270 --> 00:19:25.560
Be safe, Nami.

399
00:19:26.060 --> 00:19:29.560
[GENZO laughs]

400
00:19:29.750 --> 00:19:31.520
[DOCTOR] Take a look at this.

401
00:19:31.520 --> 00:19:34.110
[GENZO] What is it Doc... Nami's bill?

402
00:19:35.120 --> 00:19:38.160
[DOCTOR] Not exactly.
That girl will never change.

403
00:19:38.390 --> 00:19:39.450
That's her new tattoo.

404
00:19:40.210 --> 00:19:41.650
[GENZO] What's it supposed to be?

405
00:19:41.650 --> 00:19:45.250
[DOCTOR] A tangerine... and a pinwheel.

406
00:19:46.720 --> 00:19:48.000
Hey, Genzo.

407
00:19:48.220 --> 00:19:49.920
Where's your pinwheel?

408
00:19:51.760 --> 00:19:56.050
[GENZO laughs]
I don't need it anymore.

409
00:20:08.310 --> 00:20:08.940
[NAMI] I'm off.

410
00:20:10.440 --> 00:20:15.530
[baby cries]

411
00:20:16.270 --> 00:20:19.360
[BELLEMERE] Genzo, back off.
Don't get so close to Nami.

412
00:20:19.710 --> 00:20:22.660
[GENZO] I just wanted to see her smile.

413
00:20:22.680 --> 00:20:26.200
[BELLEMERE] Your face is
too scary. It's making her cry.

414
00:20:26.890 --> 00:20:29.880
[GENZO] I can't change
my face... Oh, wait...

415
00:20:30.260 --> 00:20:33.330
I'll keep this on my
hat to distract her.

416
00:20:33.330 --> 00:20:35.840
What do ya think little girl?

417
00:20:35.900 --> 00:20:37.420
[BELLEMERE] You're joking, right?

418
00:20:37.430 --> 00:20:38.760
It's just a stupid pinwheel.

419
00:20:38.770 --> 00:20:40.260
There's no way it's going to make her...

420
00:20:40.260 --> 00:20:43.810
[laughing]

421
00:20:47.170 --> 00:20:51.060
[BELLEMERE] I can't
believe it. She's laughing.

